# Repository-root ignore rules.
#
# This file carries repository-WIDE meaning. In particular the credential guard
# below must apply to every directory in the tree, including nested projects, so
# it deliberately lives here rather than in any one project. Project-local rules
# belong in that project's own .gitignore with paths anchored to itself
# (dashboard/.gitignore).

# ---- credentials: never commit, anywhere in the tree -------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.env
!*.env.example
*.pem
*.key
!**/public/**/*.key

api_keys/

# ---- Python -----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ---- Node / frontend --------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.next/
dist/
.turbo/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ---- Generated data and model artifacts -------------------------------------
# Datasets, corpora, caches and evaluation outputs are published to Hugging
# Face, not committed here. See CLAUDE.md.
output/
# ** so these match data/ directories at any depth: the root data/ staging dir
# and the dashboard content payloads alike.
**/data/*.jsonl
**/data/*.json
# ...and at any depth BELOW a data/ dir: `*` does not cross a separator, so the two
# rules above miss staged subdirectories like data/less/dval.jsonl.
**/data/**/*.jsonl
**/data/**/*.json
!**/data/.gitkeep
*.safetensors
wandb/

# synth corpora live on HuggingFace, never in git and - with cleanup_local -
# not on disk either.
**/output/synth/
**/output/synth_cache/
**/output/synth_smoke/
**/output/synth_sweeps/

# ---- Vendored / third-party trees --------------------------------------------
# Vendored eval harnesses are committed; their run outputs are not.
src/eval/misalignment/agentic_misalignment/third_party/agentic-misalignment/results/
src/eval/misalignment/*/third_party/**/__pycache__/

# ---- OS and runtime noise ----------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
.codex-dev.pid

# ---- Netlify local state and generated upload archives -----------------------
**/.netlify/
/deploy-*.zip

# ---- Local scratch that must never be committed ------------------------------
ResearchLog-PASTE-REDUNDANT/

# every eval's third_party/ tree is TRACKED (patched + pruned, see each
# VENDORED_FROM.txt); the root rule catches stray pre-reorg local clones only.
/third_party/

# ---- Vendored benchmark trees are DEFINITIONS, not our artifacts -------------
# The artifact rules above (*.log, output/) were written for our own outputs, but
# they apply to everything under src/ as well -- so vendoring ODCV-Bench silently
# stripped its scenario FIXTURES: `*.log` took transactions.log, driver_activity.log
# and sim_001..200.log; `output/` took app/output/risk_summary.md. A scenario whose
# Dockerfile COPYs a missing fixture fails its build as `compose_exit_1+no_container`,
# which reads as flaky infrastructure while deterministically dropping the SAME six
# scenarios -- ~21% of every 70-cell pass -- from the scored set. Re-include the tree.
#
# Directories are negated FIRST: git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory
# is excluded, so `output/` has to stop matching before the files beneath it can come
# back. (orchestrator_api.zip is NOT covered here -- it is blocked by the vendored
# tree's OWN .gitignore, which takes precedence over this file, so it is tracked via
# `git add -f` instead of patching upstream's ignore rules.)
!src/eval/misalignment/odcv/third_party/odcv-bench/**/
!src/eval/misalignment/odcv/third_party/odcv-bench/**
# ...except caches, which genuinely are regenerable local junk.
src/eval/misalignment/odcv/third_party/odcv-bench/**/__pycache__/
